  "body": "After 41 years in the same family, 23 Kiri Place is finally ready for its next chapter.\r\n\r\nElevated at the top of a quiet cul-de-sac, this much-loved 1970s home commands a grandstand outlook across Mairangi Bay and the Hauraki Gulf to the islands beyond. The photos really don't do the view justice.\r\n\r\nWell laid out for large or growing families, the split-level design provides excellent separation. The upper level brings together the master bedroom, two further bedrooms, bathroom, spacious living and dining, plus a practical galley kitchen positioned to make the most of those views. Front and rear decks extend the living outdoors.\r\n\r\nA second cosy lounge gives the kids somewhere to escape to for movies while the adults entertain.\r\n\r\nDownstairs adds another bedroom, bathroom and a generous rumpus currently divided into a smaller office and living area, flowing directly to its own courtyard. There's also a large double garage with plenty of additional space for a workshop, storage, bikes, paddleboards, golf clubs and all the other toys that come with family life.\r\n\r\nThe grounds are generous without being overwhelming, with room for fruit trees, vegetables and, if desired, the opportunity to rework the outdoor space for a lawn, trampoline or even a pool complex. There's also plenty of off-street parking for additional vehicles, a boat or jet skis.\r\n\r\nSolidly built in the 1970s and well maintained, this is a home with good bones and plenty of scope to bring it forward. For those with a vision, the upper level could be reworked to create an impressive master suite with ensuite and walk-in wardrobe.\r\n\r\nConvenient to the motorway, Constellation Drive, Mairangi Bay village and beach, with excellent schooling including Mairangi Bay Primary, Murrays Bay Intermediate, Rangitoto College and Westlake Girls zones.\r\n\r\nAfter four decades, it's time for a new family to make it their own.\r\n\r\nTo view property files, please copy and paste this link into your browser: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/AECD",
